{"_id":"68de95db166b018f83df7f44","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"74sme3agcXP7TRSGjYcWG","description":"# RGB Colors in CSS\n\nRGB in CSS allows you to define colors using the Red, Green, and Blue color model. You specify the intensity of each color component (Red, Green, and Blue) as a value between 0 and 255, or as a percentage from 0% to 100%. By combining different amounts of red, green, and blue, you can create a wide range of colors. For example, `rgb(255, 0, 0)` represents pure red, `rgb(0, 255, 0)` represents pure green, and `rgb(0, 0, 255)` represents pure blue.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Color","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color_value","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214502"},{"type":"article","title":"rgb function","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/rgb","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214503"},{"type":"article","title":"CSS RGB Colors","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_colors_rgb.asp","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214504"},{"type":"video","title":"CSS - Colors RGB & RGBA - W3Schools.com","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6tbUo6PXc88","_id":"6a67293033d15c8310214505"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-02T15:10:19.625Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa","6a20ca2fac1c5fa9928aa8d0","6a20cb82ac1c5fa9928aa8e3"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d7